        {
          "id": "india-gst-october-2026-11-01",
          "headline": "GST collections jump 23% to ₹2.31 lakh crore in October",
          "summary": "Gross GST revenue rose 22.9% from a year earlier, the fastest growth in more than four years, helped by a 42% rise in tax on imports. Net collections after refunds rose 25.6% to about ₹2.03 lakh crore. Part of the jump comes from a low base after last year's GST rate cuts.",
          "why_it_matters": "Strong tax receipts give the government more room to spend while oil prices stay high.",
