          "headline": "Centre sets up high-level panel to plan banking reforms for 2047",
          "summary": "Former Central Vigilance Commissioner Suresh N. Patel will chair a committee to recommend structural, regulatory and legal changes for banks. Members include RBI Deputy Governor Shirish Chandra Murmu and former RBI Deputy Governor N. S. Vishwanathan. It has six months and will also draw up a roadmap for AI and digital banking with cyber safeguards.",
