          "id": "world-iran-us-hormuz-talks-2026-11-01",
          "headline": "Iran cuts its Hormuz reopening timeline to two days as US talks go on",
          "summary": "After Qatar-mediated talks in Tehran and Qatar on 30 and 31 October, Iran's foreign minister Abbas Araghchi said a partial reopening of the Strait of Hormuz would now take two days instead of seven. Tehran wants the US naval blockade lifted, oil sanctions waived and frozen assets released. President Trump called the talks fine but said Iran was not reliable.",
          "why_it_matters": "Any reopening of Hormuz would ease the oil squeeze that has pushed Brent above $113 and kept the rupee near 95.",
